 "label_basis": "agents/retrain-policy.md judges against the current production configuration, the mean of models/gru_dst_1h_seed{0,1,2}.pt. On clean validation neither rate meets the bar: rate 1 changes overall MSE by +0.35% (95% interval -0.12 to 0.83) and storm hour MSE by -0.90% (-3.90 to 3.07); rate 0.5 by +0.27% (-0.17 to 0.72) and -1.11% (-5.01 to 1.46). No claimed gain has an interval that excludes zero.",
 "reading": [
  "Clean validation, 3 seed mean: no regime improves with an interval that excludes zero. Quiet hours get slightly worse at both rates (rate 1 +0.45%, 0.03 to 0.90; rate 0.5 +0.38%, 0.01 to 0.80).",
  "Storm and intense changes flip sign from seed to seed (rate 1 storm: seed 0 -6.58%, seed 1 +7.02%, seed 2 -0.55%), so they are seed noise at this sample size.",
  "Diagnostic only: on validation with synthetic gaps from the same gap model (blank_gaps rate 1, seed 2024, not the real ACE mask) the production GRU has 16.4% higher MSE than on clean data (RMSE 2.8270 vs 2.6205), and the candidates remove most of that: rate 1 all hours -7.20% (-8.48 to -6.05), storm -12.06% (-19.04 to -1.54); rate 0.5 all -6.50% (-7.56 to -5.51), storm -11.86% (-17.07 to -3.69). This does not decide the label; real ACE inputs were not scored.",
  "The option is kept behind --gap-aug (off by default) because it is small and reuses add_train_copies; it is not a production candidate."
 ],
